  "digest": "# INFRASTRUCTURES \u2014 sector digest, ISO week 2026-W45\n\n**Coverage changes.** No Infrastructures publication moved this week. CDIA remains the desk's only live name: REDUCE, target Rp287 against the 29 October close of Rp362, -20.5% [CDIA report]. BREN stays parked after two QC failures and the 1 November queue close, with no rating or target [fund record]. The 5 November queue refresh re-listed 65 initiations across the five industries, none started [fund record]. MTRA, one of them, is delisted on 10 November [triage 3 Nov].\n\n**Deck moves.** None, because none exists. No Infrastructures deck is built in fund record \u2014 only macro, oil, metals, agri, coal and konglo \u2014 so there is no sector spot-versus-forecast gap; the industries read only macro inputs. The macro deck refreshed USD/IDR spot to 18,003.5 on 6 November against an FY2027E path of 18,350, 1.9% below forecast [macro deck, usd_idr]. Building the sector decks remains the gate on 62 queued names.\n\n**Material news.** PGEO reported record nine-month production of 4,114 GWh, is accelerating a 105 MW geothermal project toward 1 GW by 2028, gave dividend guidance and ruled out a buyback, preferring a rights issue or divestment to lift free float from 11.2% to 12.5% by March 2027 [triage 4 Nov]. WIKA's new contracts reached Rp9.78trn to September, up 57.9%, while its nine-month net loss narrowed to Rp1.53trn [triage 1, 4 Nov]. JSMR revenue rose 7.9% to Rp15.6trn; TOWR revenue grew 14.18%; MTEL profit was pressed by operating costs [triage 31 Oct, 6 Nov]. META declared an interim dividend of Rp60.64bn, Rp3.5 a share, an estimated 1.47% yield [triage 7 Nov]. DOOH agreed to buy 6.68bn INET shares for Rp2.005trn; PORT and TOTL declared Rp100.25bn and Rp136.4bn interim dividends [triage 4-6 Nov]. ARKO was suspended; BREN left the IHSG on 2 November with OJK administrative sanctions, no criminal case [triage 2, 6 Nov].\n\n**What to watch.** The 10 November MTRA delisting; whether ARKO's suspension lifts; PGEO's free-float route and the 14 geothermal working areas on tender; TLKM, EXCL and ISAT Q3 follow-through; and CDIA's refinancing calendar into the March 2027 float step.\n\n*Research only; not a recommendation to act.*",
  "digest_file": "fund record"
}